The rule recover_json_object says: 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text.' For the input fence[ A ] B, the fence holds A, so the last object inside the fence is A; recovery is A. For the rewritten fence[ A C ] B, the fence holds A then C, so the last object inside the fence is C; recovery is C. Therefore the check's answer ought to move.